{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Vistoli: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{vistoli_hilbert}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ca8f5e34dd108e1c960963e6c56db63cdf61c718a282b7b6b74566611ef3d8b7", "source_text": "The Hilbert stack and the theory of moduli of families", "source_text_hash": "sha256:968ba89a5f435df0568b29474b29bf0a327a8a3c123fb7e82de21106d2703f01", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item001"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{H}\\text{ilb}(\\mathcal{F} / S)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{H}\\text{ilb}(\\mathcal{F} / S)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{H} \\text{om}_S(T, \\mathcal{X})$", "MATH_0007": "$T$", "MATH_0008": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:acbb8e6f50d84f06082021f5e743fa1acbc4564e1edb95e90c4fead83ca498af", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:64dc52cd93c48f2566e90aff669bb821ec1aacb5775b48969d317fbd97818071", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is a algebraic stack separated and locally of finite type over a locally Noetherian and locally separated algebraic space <MATH_0002>, Vistoli defines the Hilbert stack <MATH_0003> parameterizing finite and unramified morphisms from proper schemes. It is claimed without proof that <MATH_0004> is an algebraic stack. As a consequence, it is proved that with <MATH_0005> as above, the Hom stack <MATH_0006> is an algebraic stack if <MATH_0007> is proper and flat over <MATH_0008>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4d6efd5fc1ef5cfca8f8be5031c7da94dc1acd0e1d9126a755fc4a149d4a5b81", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item001-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Olsson, Starr: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{olsson-starr}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd1d8b89c37a8c4aac2c4c41e1be7cbfb9a79e921d9a5faa35a35ce018aa7b2b", "source_text": "Quot functors for Deligne-Mumford stacks", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a15ef292cb4eb70c2e72ce82a667174f70870f511040833446ed40cb8b2bcba5", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item002"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\text{Quot}(\\mathcal{F} / \\mathcal{X} / S)$", "MATH_0006": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:88b121deba5d22ba05a235372edacf9bbab6fbb9eac2167b3a5eca722fc349de", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0394d6894f2819bf8108c6701a2732dfe6d0b23bb1e8567d9a083c5a2bc520a9", "source_text": "If <MATH_0001> is a Deligne-Mumford stack separated and locally of finite presentation over an algebraic space <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> is a locally finitely-presented <MATH_0004>-module, the quot functor <MATH_0005> is represented by an algebraic space separated and locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0006>. This paper also defines generating sheaves and proves existence of a generating sheaf for tame, separated Deligne-Mumford stacks which are global quotient stacks of a scheme by a finite group.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:70e8effa783325c751f529607ac99b8a816cce1c5c59832ff54fbe4c7323ad4d", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item002-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Olsson: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{olsson_homstacks}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:120863f669260d33d32811683b49317323380af9b9c7e5cbeac04d910a46a450", "source_text": "Hom-stacks and Restrictions of Scalars", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c78d07e1a4898da1a634c41d0484abea91a972cee53158c42667cb6954a32b85", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item003"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\Hom_S(\\mathcal{X}, \\mathcal{Y})$", "MATH_0010": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:603b9cfb6fd933322de2003fab7744a5d253a9e6a99ad04c0711ec6f5c2cfa73", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a246ddbf4a44aa275b0dadfd4179ee6de5c9c1a00c314925b5bab81ba3257d62", "source_text": "Suppose <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are Artin stacks locally of finite presentation over an algebraic space <MATH_0003> with finite diagonal with <MATH_0004> proper and flat over <MATH_0005> such that fppf-locally on <MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007> admits a finite finitely presented flat cover by an algebraic space (eg. <MATH_0008> is Deligne-Mumford or a tame Artin stack). Then <MATH_0009> is an Artin stack locally of finite presentation over <MATH_0010>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0584aa4d145b034e62ed398feb7865533498425bb4fa8ab73b1c8d8b0610a8ab", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item003-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Alexeev and Knutson: \\emph{", "suffix": "} (\\cite{alexeev-knutson})\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3eb74371814f638518d0aa6c942d91e9499c795105a0536a4a1ebf95b43e9919", "source_text": "Complete moduli spaces of branchvarieties", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cf5c7e83f7cfa511af886b87efe2884d3274356bd7b804900b561db5bb4440f7", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item004"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {"EMPHCLOSE_0001": "}", "EMPHOPEN_0001": "\\emph{", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathbf{P}^n$", "MATH_0002": "$X \\rightarrow \\mathbf{P}^n$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$i$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:76371bd24c1ad5267a31684d949505b7ce0bbc91c88be247429bdcfccbbc96e3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f19563fa390a5aa79807341dec2bdb0a4edaf14ae4aaaade79cfd5e0f200f31", "source_text": "They define a branchvariety of <MATH_0001> as a finite morphism <MATH_0002> from a <EMPHOPEN_0001>reduced<EMPHCLOSE_0001> scheme <MATH_0003>. They prove that the moduli stack of branchvarieties with fixed Hilbert polynomial and total degrees of <MATH_0004>-dimensional components is a proper Artin stack with finite stabilizer. They compare the stack of branchvarieties with the Hilbert scheme, Chow scheme and moduli space of stable maps.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b2d1a457364031eda02c8d1c7391351a828a55527f286055afbf9df1ddced69", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item004-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Lieblich: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{lieblich_remarks}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:34bf248354fa7ca53fd6c4b033adb3f7b658bddd0ee7ab677cba6d8ee5827cbf", "source_text": "Remarks on the stack of coherent algebras", "source_text_hash": "sha256:561a9a9af8ef0cd2d971c6f686903cd00e7539ed40a5d9dd5662c7d2d7d59f2e", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item005"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$\\text{Quot}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Hom$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:67814c0a8301022ef99bb9f81061bdbfc9db8a3be3f958619bbae5b974988af5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6537f7acc4b4d125e3aaf61516d4119dbfc95f74996be3880e84199f2b28941b", "source_text": "This paper constructs a generalization of Alexeev and Knutson's stack of branch-varieties over a scheme <MATH_0001> by building the stack as a stack of algebras over the structure sheaf of <MATH_0002>. Existence proofs of <MATH_0003> and <MATH_0004> spaces are given.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:83e6b8b6130119864d856b1a40b7f35254b7c9e767e27839e587f7c94e4e282e", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item005-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Starr: \\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{starr_artin}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0e61b7b762b01f75755fd348265e143ec3c0286cdf8f7576072e6bb689143aa3", "source_text": "Artin's axioms, composition, and moduli spaces", "source_text_hash": "sha256:32dc69ec9b68834018c27909fd8cba78c6866b1e9e7391cf944a7adf3ff8cad3", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item006"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {"CITE_0001": "\\cite{vistoli_hilbert}", "CITE_0002": "\\cite{alexeev-knutson}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{H}$", "MATH_0004": "$g: T \\rightarrow \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$T$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$L$", "MATH_0008": "$S$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:adcdc2c009e31dc72dd81b24c81864832ed076e3084b4782bc0db412942af9fc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9510e6d464d8aba3b5cd4701f8e05fc93beb2830f25fab75b2e68e3099ac373e", "source_text": "As an application of the main result, a common generalization of Vistoli's Hilbert stack <CITE_0001> and Alexeev and Knutson's stack of branchvarieties <CITE_0002> is provided. If <MATH_0001> is an algebraic stack locally of finite type over an excellent scheme <MATH_0002> with finite diagonal, then the stack <MATH_0003> parameterizing morphisms <MATH_0004> from a proper algebraic space <MATH_0005> with a <MATH_0006>-ample line bundle <MATH_0007> is an Artin stack locally of finite type over <MATH_0008>.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4a1c86008223cece7a35583820293e728c2879d55b985229655b4f1850aea562", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item006-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Lundkvist and Skjelnes:\n\\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{lundkvist-skjelnes}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e43339122e1741c3ad3ccfa18a7eeb1c8bbcc77bfdb586ccd6f668ca1cbcadd8", "source_text": "Non-effective deformations of Grothendieck's Hilbert functor", "source_text_hash": "sha256:418b9b49c356c7d6d710d011b3d2e4ff3b16c6eea67032b4aabd43e1e7684546", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item007"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3c95c1f4258007ccdc737636bcabe07b8717f04fdae198cab92d06cde7242624", "source_text": "Shows that the Hilbert functor of a non-separated scheme is not represented since there are non-effective deformations.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:02db0eb19ddaae4f4dc489198989923cee36e378b9d4f20116eff0ecf1febdd8", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item007-quote"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "list_item", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\item Halpern-Leistner and Preygel:\n\\emph{", "suffix": "} \\cite{HL-P}\n\\begin{quote}\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:39be3a7620ef71a434269d4640fa5cd203f93ebea67059849500072a2e9711f9", "source_text": "Mapping stacks and categorical notions of properness", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b6546c914e457fa6a7c0ca89c2b3a7816bc4ee69a7e319d7ef3e32f12a1218b9", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item008"}
{"chapter": "guide", "node_kind": "quote", "parent_tag": "04V4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": "\n\\end{quote}\n\\end{itemize}\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fd0de28d556b88c70c17685166532b6104a3cee5b9c86152be69c1e72e0aaa60", "source_text": "This paper gives a proof that the Hom stack is algebraic under some hypotheses on source and target which are more general than, or at least different from, the ones in Olsson's paper.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fff7fd11ef19c923314e0b99b9ac60d33511172db187a4f72abeae6443348f59", "unit_id": "tag:04V4:item008-quote"}
